WEBVTT

00:00:00.316 --> 00:00:03.316
I want to talk about managing media
on your website.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.683
On the old site,

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:10.016
adding media to your content
was a two step process.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.350
We needed to add it to our media library.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.150
Copy the URL.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.150
Go to our content and embed the media.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.950
Now it's no longer a two step process
and we don't really need to manage

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.100
our media here.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.700
This is the dashboard.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.900
Media block.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.250
We can look at our media here.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.600
We can edit it.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.600
We can if we scroll
all the way down to the bottom

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.600
see more, we can search.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.550
For media.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.016
But ultimately what we want to do

00:00:46.016 --> 00:00:49.016
is add it to a

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.483
piece of content.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.483
So let's say we have a news message.

00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:58.916
And we want to add an image to it.

00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:01.350
Now something to think

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.400
about
when you're adding images to your website

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:09.833
is that the images need to have
alternative text for people with vision

00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:14.116
impairments or other impairments
that don't allow them to view the image.

00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:16.200
We don't want to leave them out.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.416
We don't want our, you know,
we want our content to reach everybody.

00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:24.833
And there's also our legal obligation
to make sure that our content

00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:28.400
is accessible
to those people with disabilities.

00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:30.716
So let's use an example here.

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:33.716
Let's say we wanted to upload this

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.800
wild cat picture.

00:01:36.916 --> 00:01:39.983
Now one issue with this picture
is that it actually contains text

00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:40.916
within the picture.

00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:44.450
So we need to make sure that all of that
text is in our alternative text.

00:02:03.016 --> 00:02:04.283
We can insert that image.

00:02:06.866 --> 00:02:09.800
And we're just

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.800
going to use this as a test.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.766
And there's our image.

00:02:19.766 --> 00:02:22.766
And if you look at the source code
you can see that

00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:26.300
when somebody comes through the screen
reader it's going to read this alt

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.300
text.

00:02:32.116 --> 00:02:35.116
So let's delete that.

00:02:35.366 --> 00:02:37.883
And take a look at another

00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:39.200
image.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.700
Let's say we wanted to post this image

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.700
about the book fair.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.900
Now as you can see, this

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:51.166
image contains a lot of text.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.800
In order to make this accessible.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.116
We would need to take all of this text
and put it in the alternative text field.

00:02:57.983 --> 00:03:00.050
That doesn't seem like
it's really a good idea.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:03.500
Because think of the experience where
somebody actually using a screen reader

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:07.133
for them to have it
go through all of this text

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.983
completely without any structure.

00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:12.016
It's going to be very difficult
for them to understand.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.083
Instead, what you should do

00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:18.083
is anytime
you have an image with text in it,

00:03:19.316 --> 00:03:22.966
you need to put the text that's
in the image, actually in the news post.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.900
Now, what you would do

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.350
is go back
to the person who created the image

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.900
and ask them for a

00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:38.250
text document,
a word document, you know, whatever

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.266
kind of design documents
they're using to create that image.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.566
And normally it will have the text in it,
you know, as the text needs to be

00:03:45.766 --> 00:03:48.766
kind of agreed upon before
the image is created.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.583
Now, failing that, now,

00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:56.400
there may be some tools that can help
